cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this code or data, please cite the LREC 2026 paper below."
title: "Semantic Label Drift in Cross-Cultural Translation"
abstract: >-
  Machine Translation is widely employed to address resource scarcity in
  low-resource languages by translating data from high-resource languages.
  This work shows that semantic labels drift during translation because of
  cultural divergence between source and target languages.
